{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::agent::Tool` supplies the name and description shown to the\nmodel. `execute` can await work using the context of the current criterion.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Tool<D: Domain, A, R>: Send + Sync {\n    fn name(&self) -> &str;\n    fn description(&self) -> &str;\n    fn execute(&self, cx: &ValidationContext<'_, D>, args: A,)\n        -> impl Future<Output = R> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The test `registered_tools_use_the_current_context_and_ordinary_node_ids` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` covers each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.Tool`.\n\n- **Name:** The test registers `Lookup(\"lookup_requirements\")`, `Inspect` and `Lookup(\"other\")`. It asserts that the tool list sent to the model has the names `lookup_requirements` and `inspect` in order. It also asserts that the `other` tool is listed on the other agent, so the model sees what `name()` returns.\n- **Description:** The test asserts that the `lookup_requirements` tool's `description` in the request equals the `Lookup` impl's `description()` string, \"Find requirement node IDs matching a name glob.\". The `Inspect` description is not asserted, but it goes through the same path, so this is not a separate gap.\n- **`execute` with the current criterion's context:** The tools run when the model calls them.\n  - The `Lookup::execute` helper reads `cx.graph()` and records the pattern. The test asserts `lookup_calls == [\"requirements.sdk.*\"]`.\n  - The same call's function output is asserted to be `json!([1, 2])`.\n  - `Inspect::execute` calls `cx.read` and `cx.outgoing_edges` on the context. The test asserts that `cx.dependencies()` contains the matching `Node` and `OutgoingEdges` dependencies. This shows the tool received the current criterion's context.\n  - The `inspect` output is asserted to be the node's content.\n- **Async `execute`:** The tools are `async fn`s that the harness awaits inside the tokio test. A malformed-argument call is also checked, with the output containing \"invalid type\".\n- **Bounds:** `Send + Sync` and the `impl Future + Send` return type are enforced at compile time. The test registers the tools through `with_tool(Arc::new(...))`, and `Lookup` and `Inspect` implement the trait.",
  "references": "065a5c9039e7921d786eb71744f716c2f36c3ef870150575f90fadd1c2f2412c",
